    {
      "id": "UgxLUP-IAs05igzt2_N4AaABAg",
      "author": "@djxjxixsmjxjskjzxn1853",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_kaXlLxQwylwuF1oNRdP6d799ctuxV5WNUxu0g6r54=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Ironically those lobsters, langoustines, coastal shrimp, brown (Dungeness) crab, spider crab and whelks would have most likely been exported to Portugal from the UK.  The UK has a VAST abundance of shellfish and around 90% of it gets exported to Spain, Portugal, France and the Far East...  It REALLY pisses me off, because we should eat more of it here, but at least it gets enjoyed somewhere.",
      "likeCount": 0,
